## Why Zigapagos

- **Zero JS by default** — pages without islands ship no JavaScript at all.
- **TSX you already know** — Preact-compatible hooks via `@z/runtime`, one
  shared runtime across all islands, `client:load|idle|visible|media|only`.
- **Native SPAs too** — one `.spa.tsx` becomes a client-routed app with
  prerendered skeletons, guards, and nested layouts.
- **Made to migrate** — `zigapagos migrate` converts an Astro project's
  islands automatically; the docs are a deterministic mapping spec an AI
  agent can follow unattended.
- **A single fast binary + Bun** — no Node, no Vite, no webpack, no lock-in.

## Get started

    mise install        # zig 0.16 + bun 1.2
    zig build
    zig-out/bin/zigapagos init
    zig-out/bin/zigapagos   # dev server with live reload

Read the docs: [islands](https://github.com/valthon/zigapagos/blob/main/docs/islands.md) ·
[SPAs](https://github.com/valthon/zigapagos/blob/main/docs/spa.md) ·
[migrating from Astro](https://github.com/valthon/zigapagos/blob/main/docs/migration/astro-to-zigapagos.md)
